Finally, I reached the top of the hill.
There was a very famous viewpoint there.
I went and stood at that viewpoint.
I looked downwards.
Below were very deep and large valleys.
Due to the summer, the trees and plants were dry.
Even then, that landscape looked very amazing.
I took out my own camera from my bag.
A man was also taking pictures there.
He was taking pictures with his own phone.
I saw his phone.
His phone cover was very strange.
I put my attention back on the landscape.
I took many beautiful pictures of the valleys.
A cool breeze was blowing there.
I kept taking pictures there for a long time.
I completely lost track of time.
Suddenly, I looked at my watch.
It was five o'clock and the sun was setting.
Now it was time to go back.
